		'pull' => 'Training at Saji begins early and follows the rhythm of a commercial kitchen. Students spend forty weeks working forty hours a week across five structured daily slots.',
		'paras' => array(  ),
		'rows' => array(
			array( 'Mise en place', '06:30 – 08:00', '', 'Deliveries arrive at our Veerkade doors before daybreak. Students inspect crates of seasonal vegetables, poultry, and whole fish against supplier invoices, rejecting any substandard stock. Each cook reviews their station prep list, sharpens carbon-steel knives on whetstones, and arranges cutting boards, pans, and seasonings for the morning. Stations are thoroughly sanitised, organised, and inspected before any cooking begins. Every student checks their knife roll and ensures their steel saji tasting spoon is ready in their sleeve pocket.' ),
			array( 'Technique class', '08:00 – 10:30', '', 'At eight o\'clock, the brigade gathers around the central demonstration bench. A chef-instructor demonstrates a specific culinary skill, such as fabricating whole round fish, emulsifying a hollandaise sauce, or laminating puff pastry dough. Students take detailed notes, observe knife grips, and ask questions before returning immediately to their individual stations to replicate the technique under direct supervision, receiving real-time corrections on stance, speed, and safety.' ),
			array( 'Family meal', '10:45 – 11:30', '', 'Kitchen culture relies on the shared family meal. Each morning, a designated student station prepares lunch for all twenty-four students and seven instructors. Cooks use kitchen trimmings, market surplus, and pantry staples to produce a balanced, nourishing meal on time. Gathering around the dining tables fosters teamwork, teaches time management under deadline, and reinforces the responsibility of feeding colleagues well before guests arrive. Students clean their own dishes and clear the dining area promptly.' ),
			array( 'Lunch service', '11:30 – 14:00', '', 'The student restaurant, The Pass, welcomes forty dining guests between 12:00 and 13:30 from Tuesday through Friday. Students work both front and back of house, plating courses to order under heat lamps, expediting tickets, and pouring water. Service runs at commercial restaurant speed, teaching composure, precision, and plate presentation under real kitchen pressure as orders are received and executed. Every plate is checked at the pass before reaching the dining room.' ),
			array( 'Debrief & clean-down', '14:00 – 15:00', '', 'Once the dining room empties, the brigade strips the kitchen. Stoves are scrubbed, walk-in coolers swept, and stainless steel work surfaces sanitised according to strict professional hygiene standards. Chef-instructors lead a quiet fifteen-minute debrief to examine ticket timing, seasoning accuracy, and kitchen waste. By 15:00, all stations are formally inspected and the teaching kitchens close until the next morning. This structured reflection turns daily mistakes into concrete technical progress.' ),
		),
		'go' => array( '/programmes/', 'Read about the four terms' ),
		'sections' => array(
			array( 'Weekly schedule and theory', 'Kitchen training runs Monday through Friday from 06:30 to 15:00. On Tuesday and Thursday afternoons from 14:30 to 15:00, debrief time includes a dedicated theory session in our upstairs lecture room. Students review recipe costing, margin calculations, ordering formulas, and food safety regulations, connecting morning stove work directly to profitable kitchen management. These forty hours each week build the stamina required in professional culinary operations.' ),
