	'programmes' => array(
		'word' => 'TERMS',
		'sub' => 'forty weeks, four plates',
		'pull' => 'Our curriculum is structured into four distinct ten-week terms that take students from foundational knife skills to live restaurant service. Students may enrol in the full diploma, a focused certificate, or single terms.',
		'paras' => array(  ),
		'rows' => array(
			array( 'Foundations', 'Term I · 10 weeks', '', 'Running weeks one to ten, Term I instils fundamental kitchen discipline and habits. Students master classic French knife cuts, including brunoise, julienne, and tourné, alongside foundational vegetable preparations, egg cookery, basic stocks, and kitchen hygiene. Instruction emphasizes knife maintenance, station organisation, and sensory evaluation using the personal tasting spoon. The term concludes with an assessment plate featuring precisely measured knife cuts and foundational vegetable preparations laid out in neat rows.', 'term-1' ),
			array( 'Stocks, sauces & fish', 'Term II · 10 weeks', '', 'In weeks eleven through twenty, Term II advances into protein fabrication and sauce making. Students scale, gut, and fillet whole round and flat fish, handle shellfish, and simmer white and brown stocks. Daily practice focuses on classic emulsions, reductions, and veloutés. The practical examination requires students to execute a pan-roasted white fish accompanied by a balanced beurre blanc and glazed seasonal greens.', 'term-2' ),
			array( 'Pastry & bread', 'Term III · 10 weeks', '', 'Weeks twenty-one to thirty immerse students in the precision of the bakeshop. Led by pastry chef Owen Achterberg, the curriculum covers sourdough fermentation, yeasted enriched breads, laminated puff pastry, choux, tarts, and custards. Students learn ingredient baker\'s percentages, dough rheology, and oven deck management. Assessment centers on producing a crisp seasonal fruit tart slice alongside a rustic, crusty hearth loaf.', 'term-3' ),
			array( 'Service & stage', 'Term IV · 10 weeks', '', 'The final ten weeks transition cooks to professional kitchen leadership. The first four weeks focus on advanced menu writing, plate architecture, food cost spreadsheets, and dining room management at The Pass. The remaining six weeks consist of an external stage placement inside one of thirty partner kitchens across Rotterdam. Students graduate after presenting a composed tasting plate of roasted vegetables, savory jus, and fragrant herb oil.', 'term-4' ),
		),
		'go' => array( '/tuition/', 'See tuition & fees' ),
		'sections' => array(
			array( 'Pastry and Bread Certificate', 'The Pastry & Bread Certificate is a twenty-week intensive programme combining Term I Foundations and Term III Pastry & Bread. Designed for aspiring bakers and pastry specialists, it pairs knife safety and kitchen physics with artisanal doughs, laminations, and entremets. Tuition is €7,900, payable in two instalments, and includes uniform kit laundering, pantry ingredients, and daily staff lunch. Graduates receive a formal certificate recognizing their technical bakery competencies.' ),
			array( 'Can working cooks enrol in a single term?', 'Experienced kitchen professionals seeking specialized skill refinement may enrol in an individual ten-week term for €3,900. Whether mastering classic stocks and fish butchery in Term II or sourdough fermentation and Viennoiserie in Term III, single-term students integrate fully into the cohort. Applicants must complete the standard kitchen trial day and interview to confirm station readiness and technical baseline.' ),
		),
