		'paras' => array(  ),
		'rows' => array(
			array( 'Marta Ilić', 'Director & hot kitchen', 'since 2011', 'Co-founding Saji Culinary School in 2011, Marta Ilić directs the hot kitchen and leads kitchen culture. Her culinary philosophy centers on economy of motion, rigorous station cleanliness, and constant tasting with the traditional saji spoon. Having spent over two decades managing European restaurant lines, Marta supervises Term I foundational cookery and senior service at The Pass, training students to execute hot food with calm precision.' ),
			array( 'Owen Achterberg', 'Pastry & bread', 'since 2011', 'Co-founder Owen Achterberg has overseen the baking and pastry labs since 2011. A master baker dedicated to classical French viennoiserie, sourdough fermentation, and modern entremets, Owen leads Term III. He emphasizes ingredient baker\'s percentages, dough hydration, gluten development, and heat distribution in deck ovens. Owen believes that baking demands scientific discipline and sensory patience, teaching cooks to listen to bread crusts and evaluate crumb structure.' ),
			array( 'Lucía Ferrer', 'Sauces & stocks', 'since 2013', 'Joining Saji in 2013, Lucía Ferrer leads Term II as specialist instructor for sauces and stocks. Her curriculum deconstructs the architecture of classic mother sauces, complex glaces, emulsions, and delicate fumets. Lucía trains students to build depth of flavor through controlled caramelisation, meticulous skimming, and careful reduction. She insists that every cook master the balance of acid, fat, and salt on the palate before sending any sauce to the pass.' ),
			array( 'Kwame Mensah', 'Butchery & fish', 'since 2015', 'Kwame Mensah has led meat, poultry, and seafood fabrication at Saji since 2015. With extensive background across European commercial kitchens, Kwame instructs students on anatomical jointing, whole carcass breakdown, and delicate flatfish filleting. His teaching focuses on knife sharpening, minimal protein waste, ethical sourcing, and safe cold-chain handling. Under Kwame\'s watchful eye, students gain confidence working with primal cuts and seasonal North Sea fish varieties.' ),
			array( 'Priya Raman', 'Garde manger & vegetables', 'since 2016', 'Leading the larder kitchen since 2016, Priya Raman instructs students in vegetable fabrication, curing, pickling, cold emulsions, and intricate salad composition. She oversees Term I knife skills, guiding students through uniform brunoise, julienne, and tourné cuts. Priya champions sustainable root-to-stem vegetable cookery, teaching students to transform peels, trimmings, and surplus greens into concentrated broths, oils, and garnishes that elevate modern culinary plates.' ),
			array( 'Henrik Dahl', 'Dining room & The Pass', 'since 2018', 'Henrik Dahl joined the brigade in 2018 to direct front-of-house service and student restaurant operations at The Pass. Henrik instructs students in dining room choreography, beverage service, ticket sequencing, and customer hospitality. He believes a complete chef must understand the guest\'s perspective. Henrik ensures that students communicate smoothly across the pass expediter line, creating seamless coordination between kitchen stations and forty seated dining guests.' ),
			array( 'Amira Haddad', 'Kitchen management & costing', 'since 2019', 'Joining Saji in 2019, Amira Haddad teaches restaurant economics, portion calculation, supplier procurement, and labor costing during theory hours. Having managed operations in high-volume hospitality venues, Amira connects kitchen technique to commercial viability. Her classes teach students how to write profitable menus, calculate food cost percentages, read supplier invoices, and minimize kitchen spoilage, ensuring graduates possess the business acumen required to sustain successful culinary careers.' ),
