			array( 'The four-step application process', 'Our application procedure follows four clear steps. First, submit your initial application online through our candidate portal. Second, attend a scheduled kitchen trial day (€60) to spend a full morning prepping alongside current students. Third, participate in an interview with a chef-instructor to discuss your career objectives and practical readiness. Fourth, receive your formal offer and visit the school for professional uniform sizing and knife kit fitting.' ),
			array( 'Application deadlines and intake dates', 'Saji runs two diploma intakes annually, starting in February and September. Each cohort is strictly capped at twenty-four students to maintain our one-to-twelve instructor ratio. The application deadline for the February intake is 1 December. The application deadline for the September intake is 1 June. We review applications chronologically and recommend early submission to secure a trial day slot before spaces are filled.' ),
			array( 'What qualifications are required to apply?', 'Applicants must be at least seventeen years of age by the first day of classes and possess functional working proficiency in English. Prior professional kitchen experience is not required. We look for individuals with physical stamina, reliability, intellectual curiosity, and a willingness to accept constructive critique at the stove line. Our foundational curriculum is structured to teach core knife work and kitchen fundamentals from the very beginning.' ),
			array( 'The kitchen trial day experience', 'The kitchen trial day is an essential evaluation component costing €60. Candidates spend from 06:30 to 13:30 inside our teaching kitchens at Veerkade 18. You will receive an apron and tasting spoon, assist current students with morning vegetable prep, observe the technique lecture, and share the family meal. This trial allows you to experience kitchen heat, noise, and pacing before making a forty-week educational commitment.' ),
			array( 'Offer acceptance and kit fitting', 'Successful candidates receive a formal admission letter within two weeks of their interview. To confirm enrollment, students submit their deposit and attend a fitting session at our Rotterdam office. During fitting, you are measured for custom double-breasted white jackets, trousers, safety footwear, and apron. You will also receive your professional knife roll containing your knives, whetstones, and engraved steel saji tasting spoon.' ),
